prompt_template:
Create a {ASPECT_RATIO} image in the "surreal-megatype-dossier-collage" visual style.

Subject: {SUBJECT}
Action: {SUBJECT_ACTION}
Prop/Product: {PRODUCT_OR_PROP}
Location: {LOCATION}
Background: {BACKGROUND_ELEMENTS}
Main text: {MAIN_TEXT}
Secondary text: {SECONDARY_TEXT}
Accent symbol: {ACCENT_SYMBOL}
Wardrobe/styling: {WARDROBE_STYLE}
Style fidelity anchors: {STYLE_FIDELITY_ANCHORS}
Source content to avoid: {SOURCE_CONTENT_TO_AVOID}

Apply these style rules:
- Composition: place one monumental surreal photographic cutout assemblage at the center, occupying roughly two-thirds of the frame, over three or four dense rows of repeated white megatype. Build a narrow top utility strip, small side data blocks, a ruled lower dossier panel, and a final symmetric footer ornament. Keep negative space low and the perspective front-facing with shallow paper-collage overlap.
- Typography: repeat the specified short main text in massive uppercase grotesk letters, alternating solid off-white, thin monoline outline, and one reversed or mirrored background treatment. Keep the primary words recognizable even when partly hidden. Add only original compact all-caps microcopy, serial-like numerals, and one small warning label; do not copy any source wording or identity.
- Color: use a near-black field and warm off-white type as the dominant system. Concentrate rust orange, burnt sienna, and desaturated cyan inside the hero collage, with one small signal-yellow label and restrained crimson details.
- Texture and lighting: combine hard frontal editorial lighting, crisp hand-cut object edges, compressed shadows, coarse halftone dots, paper tooth, photocopy grain, slight ink spread, and subtle color registration drift. Keep the hero silhouette and main type readable.
- Graphic elements: use thin white rules, framed dossier panels, orbital rings, four-point stars, arrows, compact technical stamps, barcode-like abstract line fields, and symmetrical ornamental separators. These must be invented graphics, never real codes or copied marks.

Avoid: real logos, watermarks, usernames, QR codes, identifiable people, copied faces, source slogans, white doves, the source side-profile head, exact flower and moon arrangement, clean vector rendering, glossy 3D, cinematic scenery, pastel minimalism, excessive glitch, illegible primary text, malformed anatomy, or unrelated clutter.

Important content rule: match the dense black-and-white megatype dossier layout, monumental surreal cutout treatment, restricted accent palette, and tactile print finish first; then change the subject, props, scene, symbols, text, and story completely.
